# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 7.4327e+04 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 0.5520 89.120 5.3018e+05 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~89 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 F flare 0.5760 88.645 7.0066e+05 stylized  Light rises x2.1 in 0.08 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: no breakup within 0.05 s (growth of existing pancakes). Dust groups supply 0% of the rise and 0% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
4 Y first_yield 2.7330 46.001 8.5070e+08 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 1 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
5 F flare 2.7565 45.537 2.2417e+09 stylized  Light rises x8.4 in 0.12 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 45.9 km (97% of m0); split gen 0 at 45.2 km (96% of m0). Dust groups supply 54% of the rise and 48% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
6 B first_breakup 2.7716 45.243 3.7887e+09 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x4.5 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
7 F flare 2.9033 42.674 9.3118e+09 stylized  Light rises x1.9 in 0.10 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 1 at 43.0 km (35% of m0); split gen 1 at 42.3 km (34% of m0); yield gen 1 at 40.9 km (17% of m0). Dust groups supply 19% of the rise and 33% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
8 b bump 3.1269 38.488 1.8363e+10 stylized  Small fluctuation, 73% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 1) at 38.5 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
9 P peak 3.1281 38.469 1.8438e+10 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+0.2 km from the peak of energy deposition (38.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 21.7 km/s).
10 D rolloff 3.2691 36.111 6.7605e+09 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.14 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 79% of v0, 31% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
11 - drag_overtakes_ablation 3.5241 32.634 9.9112e+08 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
12 R retirement_step 3.9081 29.034 5.3113e+07 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 19% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
13 T tail 4.0611 27.943 1.8427e+07 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
14 R retirement_step 4.3911 26.287 1.8889e+06 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 18% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
